// stimuliiq — Prisma schema.
//
// Owner: db-architect (Wave 1, docs/plans/phase-6.md task #1).
// Scope: Phase 0 (identity/access + catalog) + Phase 1 (profiles/batches/enrollments)
// + Phase 2 (commerce: orders/payments/invoices/refunds/coupons; CRM: leads/activities/
// bookings; enrollment commerce-linkage via order_id + source)
// + Phase 3 (LMS core: videos, lesson_progress, attendance, resources)
// + Phase 4 (Learning Depth: assignments, assignment_milestones, submissions,
//            assessments, assessment_questions, attempts, certificates,
//            certificate_templates)
// + Phase 5 (Marketing Website: SEO/marketing columns on programs; attribution +
//            consent columns on leads/bookings)
// + Phase 6 (Engagement: notifications, notification_prefs, notification_suppressions,
//            campaigns, campaign_templates, campaign_recipients, badges, user_badges,
//            points_ledger, forum_threads, forum_posts, forum_post_votes)
// + Phase 7 (Analytics + Hardening: materialized-view read model, analytics_mv_refresh_log,
//            export_jobs, report_schedules — see the dedicated comment blocks further down)
//
// Conventions (docs/05 §1 + CLAUDE.md §3.4/§3.6/§3.8):
// - PK: uuid v4 on every table — `@id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid`.
// - Every table carries created_at / updated_at / deleted_at (soft delete).
// - tenant_id on all business tables; `permissions` is a global catalog (no tenant_id).
// - Money stored as integer minor units (paise). No floats — money fields named *_paise.
// - Migrations are forward-only; never edit a shipped migration.
// - Partial indexes (WHERE deleted_at IS NULL) are in a separate raw-SQL migration.
//
// Phase-3 NEW TABLES (docs/plans/phase-3.md task #1, docs/05 §3):
//   videos          — 1:1 with lessons; provider + asset ref only (NO raw URL stored).
//   lesson_progress — per-enrollment-per-lesson progress tracking (resume, completion).
//   attendance      — recorded-completion attendance; live_class_id nullable (live deferred).
//   resources       — lesson attachments (table + list only; signed-download deferred P4).
//
// docs-writer note (divergence from docs/05 §3 "attendance" spec):
//   attendance.lesson_id (nullable FK → lessons) is ADDED (not in the original §3 spec).
//   This column makes recorded attendance idempotent per-lesson (enrollment_id + lesson_id
//   partial-unique on source=recorded rows) without requiring fragile date-based dedup.
//   Original §3 only had (enrollment_id, live_class_id). The extension is documented here;
//   docs-writer should update docs/05 §3 attendance row to include lesson_id (nullable).
//
// docs-writer note (VideoStatus extension):
//   docs/05 §3 videos.status listed "processing|ready"; this schema adds "errored" as a
//   third value (consistent with the plan: docs/plans/phase-3.md table "processing|ready|errored").
//   docs-writer should update docs/05 §3 videos row to include "errored".
//
// LessonProgress audit-volume decision (documented here for audit.extension.ts extension):
//   LessonProgress is a HIGH-FREQUENCY table (every progress-ping from the video player may
//   call upsert). Auditing EVERY update would produce extreme audit_log churn (same concern
//   as Session in Phase 0 and Payment/Order volume in Phase 2). Decision: LessonProgress is
//   added to AUDITED_MODELS for create and completion-transition tracking only; the backend
//   service (backend-builder Wave 4) is responsible for only writing audit rows on meaningful
//   transitions (create / status→completed), NOT on every throttled last_position_s update.
//   The audit extension fires on every Prisma update, so the backend should use a lightweight
//   "position-only" upsert path that bypasses the audited client for pure position pings, and
//   uses the audited client only on status=completed transitions. This is a seam documented
//   for backend-builder; the db-architect includes LessonProgress in AUDITED_MODELS so create
//   and completion events ARE recorded — omitting it entirely would lose the completion audit
//   trail. Alternative considered: exclude from AUDITED_MODELS and audit at service layer only;
//   rejected because it would require manual audit writes scattered in the service, harder to
//   maintain. Accepted trade-off: some high-frequency update events may write audit rows if
//   the backend-builder does not separate the "position ping" path — to be addressed in W4.

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

